[Line "King's Indian Attack (2.d3)"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Breyer Variation"]

{White sets up slowly with d3, Nd2, g3 and Bg2. Black takes a big share of the centre.} 1. e4 c6 {The Caro-Kann.} 2. d3 {A quiet system.} 2... d5 {Take the centre.} 3. Nd2 e5 {With White playing slowly, Black grabs a full pawn centre.} 4. Ngf3 Bd6 {Protect e5.} 5. g3 Nf6 {Develop.} 6. Bg2 O-O {Castle.} 7. O-O Re8 {Another defender for e5. Black is comfortable.} *
